WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
(birds chirping)

00:00:11.917 --> 00:00:14.167
(scraping)

00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:18.894
- Thousands of years in
refining super efficient,

00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:22.309
most efficient way of
doing this, I would say,

00:00:22.309 --> 00:00:24.624
just like a bicycle's
the most efficient way

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.124
to put down miles.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:29.913
Everything above and beyond this you get

00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:32.144
is a diminishing return
in energy expenditure

00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:34.835
and productivity output.

00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:37.085
(scraping)

00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:45.584
- It's like meditation in motion for me.

00:00:45.584 --> 00:00:48.315
It's just really soothing,
and it puts you in connection

00:00:48.315 --> 00:00:50.635
with the energy of the earth.

00:00:50.635 --> 00:00:52.885
(scraping)

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.438
- It's nice and quiet.

00:00:56.438 --> 00:00:58.115
I could do it when my kids were napping.

00:00:58.115 --> 00:01:00.093
I could do it in the evening.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.162
I could do it early in the morning,

00:01:01.162 --> 00:01:04.853
and I didn't feel like
I was being a nuisance.

00:01:04.853 --> 00:01:07.520
(loud scraping)

00:01:11.396 --> 00:01:14.227
- I could go through with one pass
and then I go back through

00:01:14.227 --> 00:01:16.324
two or three times, and
you just keep working it

00:01:16.324 --> 00:01:18.780
closer to the edge, so you
end up with something that,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.754
at times, depending on
the grass you're cutting,

00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:25.156
you are, you tailor the blade
to what you're cutting.

00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:27.660
(hammering)

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.671
So, if I was gonna be cutting
really thin, delicate clover,

00:01:31.671 --> 00:01:33.820
you could make this thing,
you can run your fingernail

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.209
underneath it, and it
will create a ripple,

00:01:36.209 --> 00:01:38.399
like a wave, 'cause you make it so thin,

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:41.566
but for the goldenrod and reed canary,

00:01:42.711 --> 00:01:46.209
and that tougher kind of stuff like that,

00:01:46.209 --> 00:01:47.511
that would be probably too delicate.

00:01:47.511 --> 00:01:50.020
You'd end up then fracturing it.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.687
- It feels so non-destructive
and gentle and

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:57.728
life-sustaining in a sense.

00:01:57.728 --> 00:02:00.951
When we had the lawn mower,
you just run things over,

00:02:00.951 --> 00:02:02.837
and with the hand-mower you
feel like you're a part of it,

00:02:02.837 --> 00:02:04.420
and you can see the crickets
and the grasshoppers

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.111
jumping out of the grass,
the praying mantis,

00:02:07.111 --> 00:02:08.020
you know, all of it,

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.759
it's like you're in their environment,

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:12.169
and you're not destroying them.

00:02:12.169 --> 00:02:14.419
(scraping)

00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:19.031
And when you're mowing, you
really are just focused on

00:02:19.031 --> 00:02:20.599
the sound, the grass.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:22.849
Everything else disappears.

00:02:24.087 --> 00:02:26.337
(scraping)

